{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/triaging-threads/triager-prompt.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:08:04.667797Z","id":"f30c25ae08c8cd76284fded94b6da02f0e0a32db1b8c7fc7381bb0c7fbdd2273","body":{"detail":"Same gap as reviewer-prompt.md and verifier-prompt.md: plugins/claude-code/scripts/ensure-qualifier.sh never puts qualifier on PATH ('A qualifier on PATH is never probed, used, or modified'), and the only wrapper-invocation instruction is injected into the top-level session by plugins/claude-code/hooks/session-start's SessionStart hook. triaging-threads/SKILL.md says 'For large sets, dispatch subagents with triager-prompt.md, one subsystem each,' and the brief is self-contained ('Triage these qualifier threads: `{IDS or SCOPE}`') with no inherited context. Its only command, `qualifier threads --format json` (line 4), is bare and fails with command-not-found in the plugin's default configuration.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"7ffcd9eb5884efc85e5ab5af2542daa98c0a150af7aed71887ee61f2d9e1459b"},"suggested_fix":"Have triaging-threads/SKILL.md pass the resolved qualifier invocation into the dispatched brief, or add an explicit resolution step to triager-prompt.md itself.","summary":"triager-prompt.md assumes bare `qualifier` is on PATH, which this plugin never guarantees","tags":["review","review:claude-plugin-pr14","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/triaging-threads/triager-prompt.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:17:14.839933Z","id":"ee01e2ed86d5bcecffe205c28ffee068cb5cc135f2a6c537bc0a1b6c9d4a506c","body":{"detail":"triager-prompt.md:4 runs bare 'qualifier threads --format json'. triaging-threads/SKILL.md:24-25 dispatches subagents with it for large sets and passes no wrapper path. As with the reviewer and verifier briefs, the wrapper instruction exists only in SessionStart context (plugins/claude-code/hooks/session-start:99). SessionStart does not fire for subagents (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks.md), hooks.json has no SubagentStart hook, and the plugin has no bin/ directory that would put qualifier on the Bash PATH (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins-reference.md, Standard layout).","kind":"comment","references":"f30c25ae08c8cd76284fded94b6da02f0e0a32db1b8c7fc7381bb0c7fbdd2273","summary":"confirmed: the triager brief uses a bare `qualifier` that is not on PATH inside a subagent","tags":["verified","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/skills/triaging-threads/triager-prompt.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T17:00:14.408289Z","id":"dbeb44ea79c04039062edeccf16c5504c99feb7dfd6dac397f5c736c871ca31c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9b8a0136a86980787495f1656d66840fb2d6afe6","summary":"triager-prompt.md now invokes {QUALIFIER} (line 4), not bare qualifier, and the examples run against the real binary: scripts/test-plugin.sh ok: no bare qualifier invocations in *-prompt.md files; ok: skill and brief examples run cleanly against the real qualifier","supersedes":"f30c25ae08c8cd76284fded94b6da02f0e0a32db1b8c7fc7381bb0c7fbdd2273","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
